Subject: [PATCH] freedreno: Flush the batch of a deferred last_fence on a real flush

eglCreateSync() flushes with PIPE_FLUSH_DEFERRED, which leaves the batch
unflushed but still stores its fence in ctx->last_fence. A following
glFlush() with no rendering in between then takes the "reuse last_fence"
shortcut and returns without flushing that batch, so the fence never
becomes ready. A waiter on another context (pctx == NULL, e.g.
eglClientWaitSync() from a different thread) can't flush it, and blocks
until the owner renders again.

Gecko's SharedSurface_EGLImage does exactly fCreateSync() + fFlush() on
the producer and waits on the consumer thread while holding a lock the
producer needs for its next frame, which deadlocks.

Flush the last_fence's batch when the flush is not deferred.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_context.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_context.c
index 9c0fc81..e684718 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_context.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_context.c
@@ -86,6 +86,9 @@ fd_context_flush(struct pipe_context *pctx, struct pipe_fence_handle **fencep,
     * a fence, re-use the last one:
     */
    if (ctx->last_fence) {
+      if (!(flags & PIPE_FLUSH_DEFERRED) && ctx->last_fence->batch)
+         fd_batch_flush(ctx->last_fence->batch);
+
       fd_pipe_fence_ref(&fence, ctx->last_fence);
       fd_bc_dump(ctx, "%p: reuse last_fence, remaining:\n", ctx);
       goto out;
